> 	Fastest Ascension
> 		the ascended game using the lowest number of game turns

Haven't we learned by now that high score is simply a function of how much 
time the player spends killing monsters before ascending?  (see last year's 
tournament, and the one before that, and the one before that...)

If you're going to have 13 awards that distinguish between the roles, it's 
far more meaningful to give them out based on fastest ascension time[1].  No, 
it isn't a perfect system.  Early wishes and such give a big advantage to the 
players that get them.  It wouldn't be nethack without some element of luck, 
but it is still mostly skill-based.  Furthermore, ranking by ascension time 
makes the differences between the roles meaningful, as the harder roles will 
probably take more turns.

But for the Extinctionist^W Highest Score trophy, there are essentially only 
two roles: Wizard and Non-Wizard.


[1] Possibly with a "correction" for intrinsic speed.

